{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400085-am-i-the-first-person-to-notice-this","id":1400085,"title":"Am I the first person to notice this?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-30T07:55:12-07:00","id":1400085,"title":"Am I the first person to notice this?","content":"On the official 3e map there's a marked but unlabeled location in the north-east. It's a little off, (probably about 100 miles to far north and the wrong side of the river), but I choose to believe.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/tInVngb.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Do I win a prize?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23614-zardoz","name":"Zardoz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23614_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T08:00:00-07:00","id":1400087,"title":"","content":"Can I get in the hype wagon ? I'd like to know what's going on","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T08:47:18-07:00","id":1400100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400085-am-i-the-first-person-to-notice-this?p=1400087#post1400087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I get in the hype wagon ? I'd like to know what's going on</div> </div> </div> </div>If I understand correctly OP is theorizing that the city icon circled in red is in fact an Easter egg referencing the Invisible Fortress from an earlier edition map, hence why it has no label (because it's invisible!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T09:31:21-07:00","id":1400110,"title":"","content":"oh neat. Nice little easter egg","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T09:36:14-07:00","id":1400111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400085-am-i-the-first-person-to-notice-this?p=1400100#post1400100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I understand correctly OP is theorizing that the city icon circled in red is in fact an Easter egg referencing the Invisible Fortress from an earlier edition map, hence why it has no label (because it's invisible!).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah I didn't get it was an earlier edition's map while it's kinda obvious since other cities have the same name, silly me. Thanks for the answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T09:37:46-07:00","id":1400112,"title":"","content":"And to expand a bit further, the Invisible Fortress was the location of a notable adventure from 1e - it was a manse, constructed as a secret bolt-hole in the First Age by a paranoid Twilight artificer, rendered impossible to find or remember, except to those he told the secret to. When the Usurpation went down, the Twilight and some of his Solar friends fled to the Invisible Fortress and were forgotten by the world at large. They spent the next few centuries going mad from the isolation and killing one another. Eventually, they all died off*, and the Fortress was left empty - except for all the demons. The builder had bound a Second Circle demon to defending the Fortress, and she set up shop and began producing a unique race of 1st Circle demons to help her do it.<br /> <br /> In the modern day, the magic around the Fortress has finally begun to fail, permitting it to be found after merely very difficult searching, rather than being totally impossible. So players can now go in and loot it. I've never read the adventure myself, but it has something of a bad reputation - it sounds like it was very much an old-school D&amp;D-style &quot;killer dungeon&quot;, but either ignored the reasons that doesn't really work in Exalted, or used kinda bullshit tricks to nullify the character's powers to <i>make</i> it work in that style.<br /> <br /> <br /> * One of them, Larquen Quen, was heavily rumored to be the one whose ghost became the Deathlord Mask of Winters, while another, whose name I don't remember, became the Walker in Darkness - the enmity between those two was because Larquen Quen killed the one who became the Walker, and he held a grudge. None of that is official canon in 3e, though, and I doubt they'll be referencing it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T09:43:52-07:00","id":1400114,"title":"","content":"Didn't the preliminary version of the map have multiple marked, but unlabeled locations? If I don't misremember, this can just be an artifact. On the other hand, it would be an awesome Easter Egg, so I choose to believe that it is one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T10:06:22-07:00","id":1400121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400085-am-i-the-first-person-to-notice-this?p=1400112#post1400112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of them, Larquen Quen, was heavily rumored to be the one whose ghost became the Deathlord Mask of Winters, while another, whose name I don't remember, became the Walker in Darkness - the enmity between those two was because Larquen Quen killed the one who became the Walker, and he held a grudge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Daveg Chlurion, if I recall correctly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400085-am-i-the-first-person-to-notice-this?p=1400114#post1400114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't the preliminary version of the map have multiple marked, but unlabeled locations? If I don't misremember, this can just be an artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe? Not that I recall, but it being an artifact of a location they originally had, but then removed (either a previously canon location they decided wasn't important enough, or a new location that got cut for space) would actually be my guess too. But that's such a banal and dull explanation - luckily, short of a someone in the know spilling the beans, we can all choose to believe the more entertaining theory. And in the end, isn't that the real truth?<br /> <br /> The answer, of course, is no.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23614-zardoz","name":"Zardoz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23614_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T15:50:48-07:00","id":1400412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zardoz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400085-am-i-the-first-person-to-notice-this?p=1400121#post1400121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Daveg Chlurion, if I recall correctly.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it was Meherrin who was the main suspect of being the Walker. Daveg Chlurion was a Night Caste, and the Walker in Darkness has always been portrayed as a former Zenith.<br /> <br /> I actually adapted the old Invisible Fortress adventure to 2.5e rules, and my players really enjoyed it. I played up the creepiness, paranoia, and the sheer &quot;The Shining&quot; factor of it, more so than the old-fashioned &quot;dungeon crawl&quot;, and that helped, I think. Plus for extra fun (and to give them one more suspect other than the Guardian), I also planted the hungry ghost of Ozandus Pal near his corpse in the Final Retreat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I also had them in a pretty close race with the Dragon-Bloods to get there in the first place, and with all that going on to distract them, they were much less prone to suspect the Guardian until I deliberately let them catch it in a lie, and by that time they had fed it enough Essence to make it really threatening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26206-sadric-of-ysyr","name":"Sadric of Ysyr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26206_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T07:43:27-07:00","id":1400731,"title":"","content":"I remember our dragon-blooded party went to the invisible fortress, we were in the area doing other things, heard the legend and thought 'oh that sounds cool, we should find it' and did. Of course being a bunch of overly arrogant, perpetually bickering dynasts we didn't actually achieve much except for wandering around the more accessible bits of the fortress stealing the orichalcum furnishings, chatting to the AI and feeding Sesus Lahore to the ice demons for being a bit too much of a bastard on our way out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26249-keelbreaker","name":"Keelbreaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}